  "scenes": [
    {
      "narration": "In nineteen seventy-three, the stock market fell forty-eight percent, and then it did something brutal. It stayed down for years.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "hook",
          "art": "crashChart",
          "props": [
            "chartDown",
            "fire"
          ],
          "lines": [
            "It fell 48%",
            "and stayed down."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s1"
    },
    {
      "narration": "It started as a craze. A handful of so-called can't-lose stocks known as the Nifty Fifty.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "center",
          "art": "crashChart",
          "line": "The 'Nifty Fifty'",
          "props": [
            "chartUp",
            "fire"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s2"
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "narration": "Investors paid wild prices for them, convinced they could only go up, until they didn't.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-nifty",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · Nifty Fifty"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "narration": "From peak to trough, the broad market dropped forty-eight percent, and recovering took an agonizingly long time.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "thennow",
          "kicker": "S&P 500, 1973 to 1974",
          "thenLabel": "The drop",
          "thenValue": "–48%",
          "nowLabel": "To break even (real)",
          "nowValue": "~20 yrs",
          "sub": "after inflation, two decades"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s4"
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "narration": "It became one of the longest, most grinding bear markets in modern history.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-crash73",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · 1973–74 crash"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "narration": "Adjusted for inflation, it took roughly twenty years just to get your original money back.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "crashChart",
          "big": "~20 yrs",
          "label": "to break even, after inflation",
          "props": [
            "clock",
            "chartDown"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s6"
    },
    {
      "id": "s7",
      "narration": "And by one popular measure, valuations today sit even higher than they did back then.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "multpl-cape",
          "kicker": "Shiller PE, today"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "narration": "History doesn't repeat itself, but it very often rhymes.",
